---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="MyVisaDTV is a consulting practice founded by Alexandre, based in Thailand for several years. Learn about his background and why he helps applicants with their DTV visa application."
  lang="en"
  translated
>
  <section class="border-b border-sable-light bg-papier">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-6 py-16 md:px-10 md:py-20">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4">About</p>
      <h1 class="max-w-2xl font-display text-4xl leading-tight text-indigo md:text-5xl">
        Support designed by someone who knows Thailand from the inside.
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="grid gap-14 md:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr] md:items-start">
      <div>
        <img
          src="/images/alexandre-fondateur.jpg"
          alt="Alexandre, founder of MyVisaDTV"
          class="w-full rounded-lg object-cover shadow-sm"
          width="922"
          height="1229"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="font-sans text-base leading-relaxed text-encre/90">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-indigo md:text-3xl">Alexandre, founder of MyVisaDTV</h2>

        <p class="mt-5">
          I've lived in Thailand for several years, and I've been travelling across the
          country for over a decade. Even before settling here for good, I saw how
          Thailand's administrative procedures — visa matters in particular — could become
          an obstacle, or even a reason to give up, for otherwise perfectly solid plans.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5">
          The Destination Thailand Visa has changed things for many profiles: remote
          workers, freelancers, spouses of Thai nationals. But the scheme remains technical,
          evolving, and hard to navigate alone if you don't know how the Thai
          administration works or what the consular authorities expect in detail.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5">
          I created MyVisaDTV to put this on-the-ground knowledge to work for applicants
          preparing their move. My role isn't to promise a result I don't control — the
          final decision always rests with the Thai authorities — but to help you avoid the
          mistakes that slow down or weaken a file, and to stay by your side through to the
          decision.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-10 rounded-lg border border-sable-light bg-jade-bg p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg text-indigo">Why work with MyVisaDTV?</h3>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-encre/80">
            <li>— On-the-ground knowledge, not just regulatory text.</li>
            <li>— A single point of contact, reachable through to the decision.</li>
            <li>— An honest approach: we also tell you what the DTV doesn't allow.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-10">
          <a href="/en/fiche-renseignement/" class="btn-primary">Let's talk about your project</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
